9,551/8,888/11,546.

Renders the REAL Home card (src/pages/Index.tsx) and the signed-out sidebar
through @testing-library, and reads both figures out of the RENDERED DOM. jsdom
ships no IntersectionObserver and the card's entry animation constructs one, so
a never-firing stub is installed in beforeAll; without it the tree throws before
anything renders.

MUTATION CONTROL (C-34), 2026-09-03: with the Home card's primary reverted to
contributor_score, the gate fails -
  expected [ 9551, 8888, 11546 ] to deeply equal [ 7055, 6978, 6823 ]
  expected [ 9551, 8888, 11546 ] to not include 9551
Restored; 5 passed. The instrument can fail on the defect it exists to catch.

Two bugs in the harness itself, caught by running it rather than reasoning
about it, both recorded in the file: an unanchored primary pattern also matched
the wrapper, whose textContent is both lines concatenated; and digits() over
"✦ 7,055 30d" returned 705530 because the label's own digits joined the figure.

THE ELLIPSIS IS NOT ASSERTED and cannot be: jsdom performs no layout,
clientWidth/scrollWidth are always 0 and text-overflow is never computed. The
MECHANISM is asserted from the rendered DOM instead - the name element carries
truncate and its flex parent carries min-w-0, the half that silently disables
truncation when removed.

SUBSTITUTED proves the CARD, never the lane. It does not replace the production
reading after promotion and must not be recorded as one.

